{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgtJeYpijdti1dcJuu4cB","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Many mid-layer MLP neurons (layers 8–15) shift consistently in loops in both texts, by ~1.6–1.85 standard deviations. Layer 19 neuron 11 is the strongest in raw terms: its activation goes from −0.3 before the loop to −2.8/−3.0 inside it. So many neurons share the shift. That pattern suggests a distributed \"I am repeating\" state, probably a residual-stream direction, rather than a few dedicated neurons. If such a direction exists and is common to both loops, I can ask what writes it and what reads it. A positive feedback loop of the form \"detect repetition → strengthen copying\" would be a specific, repairable mechanism. Next I'll compute, per layer, the mean residual-stream difference between loop and pre-loop tokens in each text and the cosine similarity between the two texts' difference vectors. A high cross-text cosine, especially in middle layers, means a shared loop-state direction.\n\n```python\n# Hypothesis: a shared \"loop-state\" residual direction exists (high cross-text cosine of loop-minus-preloop mean diffs).\ndirs = {}\nfor l in range(24):\n    Hl = np.load(D5 + f'hidden_{l}.npy', mmap_mode='r')\n    ds = []\n    for b in range(2):\n        L = lens5[b]; on = loop_start_tok[b]\n        X = np.asarray(Hl[b, :L], dtype=np.float32)\n        d = X[on+64:L].mean(0) - X[150:on].mean(0)\n        rms = np.sqrt((X[150:L]**2).mean())\n        ds.append((d, np.linalg.norm(d) / (rms * np.sqrt(1024))))\n    cos = ds[0][0] @ ds[1][0] / (np.linalg.norm(ds[0][0]) * np.linalg.norm(ds[1][0]))\n    dirs[l] = (ds[0][0] + ds[1][0]) / 2\n    print(f'layer {l:2d}: cos(textA,textB)={cos:.3f}  |d|/|x| A={ds[0][1]:.3f} B={ds[1][1]:.3f}')\n```"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":5544,"cache_read_input_tokens":99352,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":5544},"output_tokens":7,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"37ae3ac5-393a-4da3-8caf-f8ba0ea8f929","uuid":"e44aa897-d333-4d36-af15-59fdc86fbc01","timestamp":"2026-11-10T00:31:50.162Z","request_id":"req_011CgtJeWxcB78JG9J8gEfZx"}
